  "ingredients": [
    "6 boneless pork chops",
    "0.5 cup soy sauce",
    "0.25 cup brown sugar",
    "2 tablespoons lemon juice",
    "1 tablespoon vegetable oil",
    "0.5 teaspoon ground ginger",
    "0.125 teaspoon garlic powder"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/g1qvK-SCaaPgy6HqsYEAaMlnl9k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/72007-chinese-pork-chops-step-1-2974-27f7e1751dbf4c3cad7ca1528da5408f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/72007/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pierce pork chops on both sides with a fork.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/0jurRIGVLtGiIVPn9FDpqVEUoY0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/72007-chinese-pork-chops-step-3-2983-a187e9d6f0024809bb7d0ede5a2cecde.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/72007/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk soy sauce, brown sugar, lemon juice, oil, ginger, and garlic powder together in a bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/VV37nnAuqbKGg03LTMPeBYcP6C4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/72007-chinese-pork-chops-step-2-2976-36cde6ed1f6a4d999174e7c8b60c86b7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/72007/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reserve about 1/4 cup marinade for basting; pour remaining marinage into a resealable plastic bag. Add pork chops to the bag, coat with marinade, squeeze out excess air, and seal the bag. Marinate in the refrigerator for 6 to 8 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vTax_MUuuNutM55mPJKhR4kzGYU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/72007-chinese-pork-chops-step-4-2987-9188b3ae3faf4ffaaf7d4c2ab01b2d75.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/72007/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "When ready to cook, preheat an outdoor grill for high heat and lightly oil the grate. Remove pork chops from marinade and shake off excess. Discard remaining marinade.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pork chops on the preheated grill, basting often with the reserved marinade, until no longer pink in the center, 6 to 8 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JFKHnApG5dIe-uJ31FJZ-3Y64rQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/72007-chinese-pork-chops-step-5-3099-f8675932ecd64e71932ff5e6e99b7586.jpg"
